[COMMENTS]
STATION,North-West London station located in the urbanised middle reaches of the River Brent. GENERAL: Flat V profile weir in a culvert (below Olympic Way Wembley). Following modifications to the structure in 1978, it was refurbished but the crest is sub-standard. STATION HYDROMETRY: Not originally designed as a measurement structure but as a method of hydraulically reducing the head to allow free conveyance under the culverts supporting beams. The station was reviewed in 2010. A discharge point, that entered the channel immediately d/s of the weir, compromised gaugings. Approach conditions not ideal in high flow. One rating applied across period of record. The structure is non-standard and a few gaugings suggest that the theoretical rating may not be applicable especially in peak flow range. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2024 (WINFAP Files v13). FLOW REGIME: Responsive regime.
CATCHMENT,A largely impervious urban/suburban catchment in West London.
Qmed Suitability,All flows remain within the culvert which is over 2m high. However, there are no gaugings in the peak flow range and the theoretical rating cannot be validated.
Pooling Suitability,Station can be unreliable at the most extreme flows and there is low confidence in the rating.
[END]
